---
layout: base
permalink: /index.html
title: 'Ghurab — Robotics, Autonomous Systems & Cybersecurity'
description: 'Ghurab is a robotics, hackathon, and CTF competition team building toward autonomous systems, industrial robotics, and cybersecurity. See the work, read the blog, or back us early.'
---

<div class="wrapper">
  <!--
    Cold open -> hero. One .cover viewport-height flex container with a
    single [data-centered] child (the hero-lockup), per the contract
    documented in compositions/cover.css. Shard geometry + flight paths
    come from _data/coldOpenShards.js; each shard is a CSS clip-path
    triangle over the single ghurab-mark.png raster (assets/images/brand),
    not true SVG -- there's no vector version of the mark to animate, and
    this achieves the same "assemble from fragments, no heavy JS/video"
    brief from the roadmap using plain CSS animation (see home.css).
  -->
  <div class="cover">
    <div class="hero-lockup flow" data-centered>
      <div
        class="cold-open"
        aria-hidden="true"
        style="--mark-url: url('{{ '/assets/images/brand/ghurab-mark.png' | url }}')"
      >
        {% for shard in coldOpenShards %}
          <div
            class="shard"
            style="clip-path: polygon({{ shard.clip }}); --fly-x: {{ shard.flyX }}px; --fly-y: {{ shard.flyY }}px; --rot: {{ shard.rot }}deg; --delay: {{ shard.delay }}s;"
          ></div>
        {% endfor %}
        <div class="cold-open__eye"></div>
      </div>

      <p class="hero-wordmark font-display hero-fade-in" style="--hero-delay: 1.3s">{{ meta.siteName }}</p>
      <p class="hero-motto hero-fade-in" style="--hero-delay: 1.4s">{{ meta.motto }}</p>

      <!--
        Hero line (chosen, supersedes the three candidates in spec S8).
        Note it's the English rendering of the motto directly above it, so
        the lockup reads as Latin -> English rather than as two unrelated
        lines. Worth keeping that pairing in mind if either ever changes.
      -->
      <h1 class="hero-headline font-display hero-fade-in" style="--hero-delay: 1.5s">
        Intellect governs power
      </h1>

      <p class="hero-subline hero-fade-in" style="--hero-delay: 1.6s">{{ meta.siteDescription }}</p>

      <div class="hero-links cluster hero-fade-in" style="--hero-delay: 1.7s">
        {#- Plain absolute paths, no `| url` filter: Eleventy 3 applies
           HtmlBasePlugin by default, which already rewrites href/src with
           --pathprefix at transform time. Adding `| url` here prefixes a
           second time and produces /ghurab/ghurab/blog/ on GitHub Pages. #}
        <a class="button" data-button-variant="primary" href="/blog/">Read the blog</a>
        <a class="button" data-ghost-button href="/projects/">See the work</a>
        <a class="button" data-ghost-button href="/services/">Hire us</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Three pillars. Heading is visually hidden -- three named cards read
       fine on their own, and the spec calls for terse/no elaboration here. -->
  <section class="region" aria-labelledby="pillars-heading">
    <h2 id="pillars-heading" class="visually-hidden">Focus areas</h2>
    <div class="grid" data-layout="thirds">
      <div class="pillar flow">
        <h3 class="font-display">Autonomous Systems</h3>
        <p>Unmanned platforms — ground, air, and water.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar flow">
        <h3 class="font-display">Industrial Robotics &amp; Automation</h3>
        <p>Precision engineering for real-world deployment.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar flow">
        <h3 class="font-display">Cybersecurity</h3>
        <p>Offensive-minded security research and testing.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!--
    Track record: real competition results (spec S11 resolved for competitions).
    Nothing here is invented -- every placement is an outright 1st, confirmed
    by the team. Cards use the filled (solid + cyan edge) variant, not the
    dashed "fill me in" state. Ordered strongest-first: the WRO card carries
    the full story, the other two stay terse so the detail reads as earned.

    Hackathon and CTF cards are intentionally absent until real results land
    -- card count is arbitrary (see home.css), so add them then rather than
    showing empty placeholders in front of the spec S3 audience.
  -->
  <section class="region flow" aria-labelledby="track-record-heading">
    <h2 id="track-record-heading" class="font-display">Track Record</h2>
    <div class="grid" data-layout="thirds">
      <div class="track-record-card" data-filled>
        <p class="track-record-card__label">Robotics · WRO 2026</p>
        <p class="track-record-card__entry">
          <strong>World Robotics Olympiad 2026 — National Round, Future Engineers.</strong>
          Top-performing national team in the world for the round, and the fastest open-round lap in the
          competition's history — on a robot built in half a week at a quarter of the field's cost.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="track-record-card" data-filled>
        <p class="track-record-card__label">Robotics · Cybernauts 2026</p>
        <p class="track-record-card__entry">
          <strong>Cybernauts 2026, North South University — 1st, Combat Robotics (Sumo).</strong>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="track-record-card" data-filled>
        <p class="track-record-card__label">Robotics · IUT Techathon 2025</p>
        <p class="track-record-card__entry">
          <strong>IUT Techathon 2025, Islamic University of Technology — 1st, Line-Following Robotics.</strong>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!--
    Sponsorship CTA. Copy, fields, and button label are verbatim from spec
    S8. Production is GitHub Pages, which serves static files and runs no
    server, so the form POSTs to Web3Forms using the access key in
    _data/meta.js (web3formsKey).

    While that key is empty the form renders disabled with a visible notice,
    rather than looking functional and dropping every submission on the
    floor -- a dead sponsor form in front of the audience in spec S3 is
    worse than an obviously-unfinished one.
  -->
  <section class="region" aria-labelledby="sponsor-heading">
    <div class="sponsor-cta flow">
      <h2 id="sponsor-heading" class="font-display">Back Us Early</h2>
      <p>
        Ghurab started as a competition team — robotics, hackathons, CTFs — and is building toward advanced robotics
        and autonomous systems. We're looking for sponsors who want in before this becomes a company, not after.
      </p>

      {% set formId = "sponsor" %}
      {% set formSubject = "Ghurab — new sponsor inquiry" %}
      {% set reasonLabel = "Area of interest" %}
      {% set reasonOptions = ["Sponsorship", "Partnership", "Press", "Other"] %}
      {% set submitLabel = "Become a Sponsor" %}
      {% set showMessage = false %}
      {% include "partials/inquiry-form.njk" %}
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

{% css "local" %}
  {% include "css/home.css" %}
{% endcss %}
